WEBVTT

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.720
Ah, this type of electrical interference...

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.060
It can't be...with that simple of a circuit...

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.030
A bomb?!

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:07.790
Yes, most likely.  There doesn't appear to be just one, either.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:12.290
Princess Charlotte and Teppei are still inside, correct?

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.290
That's correct.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:21.260
The vaccination we administered was mostly successful in wiping out the DNA virus,

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:28.180
but a new strain of virus has appeared and is running amok.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.140
It's due to my carelessness.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:32.940
Another unexpectedly difficult discussion, eh?

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.900
I don't fully understand it, either.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.360
Stop blaming yourself.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:41.740
If you hadn't acted, we would still be trapped at the Hills.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.410
What options do you have now?

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:48.280
I can only talk to Teppei-sama by radio.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:52.410
I am currently unable to hack into the Hills' network.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:55.290
Can you confirm how many bombs there are?

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.250
Five, at the very least.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.840
Arima Hills will collapse.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:04.550
If that happens, controlling the spread of information will become impossible...

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:08.470
No way...  If the Hills explodes...  Turn back!

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:13.140
Calm down, Houjouin!  If you panic here, nothing good will come of it.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.390
Then you're telling me to abandon the two of them?

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.690
I never said anything like that!

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.940
Stop it, you two.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.480
We should concentrate on helping them first.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.200
Damn it, here too?

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.000
Teppei...I...

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.540
I find holding your hand is kinda fun!

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:38.540
Huh?

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.380
"A date at the Hills".  Just like our promise, right?

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:43.670
W-Wait a second, Charl.  Do you understand our situation?

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:46.430
A bomb has been set up in the Hills, right?

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:47.970
You understand, and still...

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.180
It'll be okay!  You'll definitely be able to do something!

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.480
Oh dear.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.560
Can you hear me?  Son of Arima Isshin.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.570
What did you think of our dinner date?

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:02.820
You...

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.190
What are you doing?

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.200
Why are you doing this to us?

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.950
"Why?"

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:10.660
Because you're rich.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.620
We merely wish to make a withdrawal from the bank known as "good fortune".

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.420
That's all.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:21.540
Well then, I wish the two of you a wonderful evening.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.340
Hey!  <i>Hey!</i>

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.350
What's wrong?

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:34.390
It's no good.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.770
Is there no other way?

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.020
There is one.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.150
Really?

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.440
That "way," is...?

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:48.990
To reformat the entire Arima Group's servers, including those at Arima Hills.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.320
However, if you do that...

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:55.330
Yes.  We would completely erase the virus,

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:58.580
but all Arima Group data would also disappear.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.250
Yuu.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.170
Yes.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:15.600
Once you purge the virus from the servers, how long until we regain control of the Hills' systems?

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:18.230
Twenty minutes...

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:19.980
...no, fifteen!

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:21.940
Then reformat them.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.650
Cut the power.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.190
But, Milord!

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.530
I don't care!

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:31.320
Arima's data is not important now.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.160
A backup of everything exists here,

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:38.620
and most definitely inside everyone else who works for Arima.

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:43.500
Understood.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.840
It appears one of the bombs has been found.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:50.840
It's a time bomb initially set for one hour.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.590
It's a standard wired type.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.350
Twenty five minutes and thirty seconds remaining!

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:03.480
Those red circles...are those the locations of the bombs?

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:08.650
For simple devices such as these, disarming them won't be too difficult.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.240
The problem is that we're racing against the clock here.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:12.740
Give us a detailed explanation.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:18.120
The amount of time we have between cutting the power to regaining control is ten minutes.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.750
After that, there will only be ten minutes left until the bombs go off.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:24.630
For the bombs in the art gallery and shopping mall,

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:27.340
SP personnel are nearby and can make it there in time.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:33.840
However, they won't be able to reach the devices located on the hotel floor and mall floor in time.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:36.600
All right.  I'll go to the hotel floor.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:37.760
Eh?!

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:40.680
If you enter from the roof, you can make it there in time.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:41.810
Silvie!

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:45.650
Father, Charlotte is a precious childhood friend of mine,

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:51.990
and Teppei is an important friend, as well as my fiancé.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:53.240
Silvie...

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:55.660
I'm going.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.540
Hey, wait!

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.460
As if I'd let you be the only one to act cool!

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:04.500
I'm going too!

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.550
The last one is located here.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.800
SP personnel are not in this area,

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:20.010
and once we've regained control, they won't have time to reach it.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.640
Teppei-sama.

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:24.270
I heard everything.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:29.190
For placing you in such danger, Teppei-sama, I will atone as much as it is necessary.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:36.450
Please disarm the last bomb, which is on the mall floor!

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.490
I understand.  I'll do as you say, Yuu-san.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.040
Teppei-sama...

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:44.250
Formatting!

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:46.330
Beginning format.

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:03.930
Ah, we've been left behind.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.180
I wonder where this is?

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.520
You idiots!  Hurry up and get out of there!

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:08.900
Yes.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.310
I'm sorry.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:12.270
Hey, it's Arima Teppei!

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.400
Eh, along with the perverted princess!

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.610
Huh?  You're the two from earlier?

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:18.660
You know them?

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.410
Nope, they're bad guys.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:21.120
Eh?!

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.370
They're pretty nice, though.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.870
Which is it?

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.960
A rendezvous with a good-looking guy and a princess holding hands?

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:33.210
That kind of situation never happens in reality!

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:34.300
You're unforgivable!

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:38.800
Stop it!  Please, let us go!

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:43.720
She's so cute!  I want to take her home!

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:46.350
I can imagine her in an apron...

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:51.150
Oh, that's great.  I'd have her wear my country's national dress.

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.730
You're a nutcase.  Well, then, it's got to be a naked apron!

00:08:57.860 --> 00:08:59.410
Don't think about her like that!

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:01.990
Sorry!  Bye bye!

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.700
Damn it, attacking us when we were in the middle of a conversation...

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:10.210
Still, it would be nice if we could meet again.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:17.260
Damn it!  No good here, either.  The shutter is still closed!

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:21.050
Teppei-sama, if you cannot get through, you will not make it in time!

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.640
Please try breaking through somehow!

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:25.010
Break through?

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:27.140
There is no other way!

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.270
Charl, stand back.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:30.350
Okay!

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:37.940
Teppei!

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.530
What is with this thing?!  It didn't even budge!

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:44.780
It was designed not to give way under extreme stress.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:47.750
You told me to do "something" about it, knowing that?

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:48.200
Yes.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:51.040
Even if you tell me that...

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.170
Maybe I should go with this?

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.630
I've been waiting for that!

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:58.260
I'm excited, excited, excited!

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:58.260
Why do you look so happy?

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:02.510
Huh?  That sword is made of wood, right?

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:04.090
Er, yeah.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:05.260
Can it cut?

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.270
I guess I won't know until I try!

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:11.100
How's that?

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:18.530
Charl!

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:23.320
Ah, Charl, I'm sorry!  I'm sorry!

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:23.820
Are you okay?

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.780
You're not hurt, are you?  You're fine, right?

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:27.740
Oh my goodness, I'm so sorry!

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:40.970
Hey, is it all right if I talk to you now?

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:43.390
Aren't you already talking to me?

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.220
Well, I guess that's true.

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:46.560
What is it?

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.810
Just now, you said,

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:51.100
"Teppei is my fiancé," right?

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:57.440
Weren't you acting a little impudently?  That's against the "Hot Spring Pact", you know.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:00.990
I don't even know, myself.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:07.750
I loved my Mom.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:11.210
What's that about?  Is that related to our conversation?

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.250
My feelings are the same as they were back then.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.630
When Mom died, I didn't cry.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:24.220
I was devastated, but the tears just wouldn't come out.

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:29.730
Even so, I was always calling out my mother's name in my heart.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:33.560
Does that mean you love Teppei as much as you loved your mother?

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:37.780
I don't want to experience those feelings ever again.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:42.360
I was young at the time, so I couldn't do anything.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:46.160
However, there is something that I can do now.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:48.620
In other words, you like him.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.250
I like Teppei.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:56.550
He irritates me, and is hopeless at so many things...

00:11:57.170 --> 00:12:00.380
Still, I fell in love with him before I knew it.

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:06.560
You're able to state your feelings so clearly.  I envy you.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:13.150
I really don't envy you and Charl being nobility and royalty, but...

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:17.320
...it must be painful being unable to admit who you like.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:19.610
You're probably right.

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.990
Go, go, Teppei!

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.660
You can do it, Teppei!

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:29.240
Yay, yay, Teppei!

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.240
Charl, give me a hand here.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:30.580
Okay!

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:37.420
Charl, where did you get that?

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:40.670
Over there, from the Danhel brand shop.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:42.970
Seriously, they sell things like that?

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:45.970
Hey, wait up!

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:56.360
Hartman was Princess Charlotte's fiancé, correct?

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:57.360
That's right.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:00.320
Regarding Hazelrink...

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.740
Of course.  This is something that we must tell them.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:08.620
Before that, it's logical to allow the Princess to speak to them first.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:16.500
Lady Silvia's and Princess Charlotte's childhood bond is strong.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:19.590
Even if he were still alive,

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:23.970
certain people would bear a grudge against him for living such an honest life,

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:26.470
it's sad to say.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:29.510
I can't stand how cruel the world can be at times.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:31.060
You're right.

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:32.890
Purging of the virus, complete!

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.940
Restoring electricity to Arima Hills.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:38.610
Ten minutes remaining until time's up!

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:45.530
All right, they're on every channel!  This is good enough, for a start.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.450
Those women can wait until after we're done!

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.370
Like I said, don't call them, "those women"!

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:51.620
I get it, I get it!

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.040
We've regained control of all systems!

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:59.170
W-Wait!  You're going too fast!

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:00.840
We got through!

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:05.170
Teppei-sama, go straight ahead and follow the hallway as it curves!

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:06.010
Got it!

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.090
Let's go, Charl.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.090
Yeah!

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:23.360
Art Gallery here, the bomb has been defused.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.780
Shopping Mall, the bomb is defused.

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:27.360
There it is.

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.950
Hey, there are only two minutes left!

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.870
We've found the bomb.  Please, give me instructions!

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:35.120
First, please remove the casing.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.500
This is what you would call a "wire dilemma" type of bomb.

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:42.000
"Wire dilemma"?  Hey, aren't you scared at all?

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.550
We've already come this far, being scared is pointless now.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:47.300
Ah, I've got a really bad feeling about this.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:52.970
There should be three wires.  You absolutely must not cut the yellow one because it is a dummy wire.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:57.640
The problem is: red or blue.  Until you cut one of them, we have no way of knowing which is the correct one.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:01.100
As I thought!  Why tell us just now?!

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:04.150
I see.  That's why it's called "wire dilemma".

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:06.530
Hold this.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:09.530
Thanks.  Wait, why am I holding it?!

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:12.620
Hold it, please.  I'll think about which one we should choose.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.740
Think?  How?!

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.210
Why are you looking away?!

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:21.080
Stop your whining and let me concentrate.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.590
Blue.  Blue, right?  It looks like it's a new string.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.800
You're Arima Teppei, right?

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:32.510
The next one will hit.

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:35.220
Did you run away from your comrades?

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:42.940
I received information from my comrades.  They told me that Arima Teppei was with the Princess.

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:44.560
I've heard about you.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:48.440
You became the heir to the Arima Foundation almost overnight.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:53.160
I figured you would be stubborn and come to rescue the Princess.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:56.620
It is indeed a fascinating story.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:59.540
So why are you pointing a gun at us?

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.120
It's because you're an eyesore.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:04.130
All those who are loved more,

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:05.500
noticed more,

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:08.800
and excel more than I do are eyesores.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:11.340
The Boss told me not to interfere,

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:15.350
but when you just appear right in front of me, I get a little anxious.

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.350
My next shot will hit you.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.310
Using something like a gun...

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.810
What do you expect to do with that broken wooden sword?

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:26.110
That can't win against a gun.

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:28.400
Charl, take cover.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:29.570
Teppei?

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:31.610
I'll be fine, no matter what.

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.200
Damn it!

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:48.840
I don't need a wooden sword to deal with you.

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:54.220
Real men express their feelings with their fists!

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:57.970
I'm sorry.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:03.690
I had something else I wanted to say, but my head is a bit mixed up now.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:07.400
Let's go.

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:09.440
We have to save everyone.

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:10.690
Yeah.

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:16.030
Hey, there's no time left!

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:17.070
It's hopeless!

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:22.200
I can't take it anymore!

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:30.250
Which one did you cut?

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:31.550
Red.

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:35.050
It's not stopping!

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:37.430
I told you, "blue", didn't I?

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:39.350
Huh?

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.930
I-It stopped.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.230
As I thought.

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:45.770
"As I thought"?  What do you mean?

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.690
It's my lucky color for today.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.360
In other words, you guessed?

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:50.940
It wasn't a guess.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:54.950
Coincidentally, the underwear I'm wearing today is red, too.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:56.200
I see.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:58.910
<i>What!? Only ten seconds!?</i>

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:00.620
Damn it!

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:01.410
Teppei!

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.330
<i>The trash chute!</i>

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:18.720
We're saved.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.140
Teppei-sama?

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:22.850
I threw it in the trash chute...

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:24.980
That was a wise decision.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:30.150
The Arima Hills trash chutes are made of solid steel seven inches thick.

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:32.270
What's with that?

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:34.610
Teppei!

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:37.740
You were amazing!  That's my Teppei!

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:40.450
Charl, this is the men's restroom.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:51.960
You did well.  It's all thanks to you.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:54.670
I don't deserve those kind words.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:57.510
Besides, the ones who did their best are

00:18:57.720 --> 00:18:59.220
Silvia-sama, Houjouin-sama,

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:00.300
Silvia-sama, Houjouin-sama,

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:04.180
Teppei-sama, and Charlotte-sama,

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:08.060
and everyone from the Arima SP.

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:12.440
Yes.  Everyone, you were excellent.  Thank you.

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:17.280
I, Arima Isshin, am grateful from the bottom of my heart.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.410
Everything is fine now.  Please, rest.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.370
Thank you very much.

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:28.790
Everyone's safe and sound!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:29.500
Well, yeah.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:33.290
I'm glad, I'm really glad!

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:37.260
Thank goodness.  Thank goodness.  Thank goodness.  Th---

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:36.210
Charl.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:39.300
Please calm down and listen to me.

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:40.970
What is it?

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.220
Hartman...it seems that he was killed.

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:45.220
Hartman...it seems that he was killed.

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:51.850
Hey, why are you bringing it up now...?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:55.770
He tried to save my father and Arima Isshin.

00:19:58.150 --> 00:20:00.280
I see.

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:06.870
He tried to save your father and Isshin-sama.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:07.990
Yes.

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:10.290
That makes me happy.

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:16.540
To tell the truth, I didn't really like him at first.

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:19.550
Still, since it was decided he'd eventually be my husband,

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:23.590
I always tried my best to like him.

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:32.560
The fact that he tried to save Silvie's father and Isshin-sama in the end makes me happy.

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:34.350
I've finally...

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:39.110
...come to like him.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:49.120
Charlotte-sama.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.750
We have heard all the details from Arima-sama.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:55.670
Now, if you would please return to the mansion.

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:57.920
Um...how's Alf?

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:01.670
We plan to hide what happened tonight from Alfred-sama.

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:04.630
We musn't worry him.

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.590
I see.

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:08.050
Thank you.

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:11.020
Then I'll see you later.

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:12.520
Tomorrow at school, like usual?

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:13.890
Yeah.

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:14.850
See you later.

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:16.690
Be careful.

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:19.190
Teppei, thanks a lot!

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.650
Teppei, thanks a lot!

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:29.410
She finally came to like him after he died.

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:32.830
That's...kind of sad, isn't it?

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:41.460
It was wise of her to say that with a smile.

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:45.130
Charl isn't the type of person who can hate somebody.

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:27.470
Question!

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:31.600
The Arima Hills shutters and trash chutes are made of steel seven inches thick,

00:23:31.810 --> 00:23:33.640
but what if an explosion really occurred?

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:35.640
Just the shutters and trash chutes would remain.

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:38.190
Next time, on Princess Lover!  Loss and Rebirth!

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:40.480
Note: hayashiraisu is hashed meat with rice.

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:40.480
Those and hashed meat with rice would be all that remained.
